                                                "sense_id": "fd6d01e2-faf4-31f1-8b0f-7717a601ad29",
                                                "text": "All in a hot and copper sky, / The bloody Sun, at noon, / Right up above the mast did stand, / No bigger than the Moon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb6e21e7-df27-4990-8a14-ad4dcbb438c4",
                                                "sense_id": "fd6d01e2-faf4-31f1-8b0f-7717a601ad29",
                                                "text": "She seemed so alive, with her shining eyes and her copper hair and her jokes and funny stories, but there was always a mystery at the center of her life, the sound of wild sobbing my mother said she heard coming through the floor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
